values ('b6c7d8e9-0f1a-4c16-9d56-6e7f8a9b0c66', 'anthropological-theory', 'Anthropological Theory', 'This course surveys the major theoretical traditions, disputes, and contemporary turns that have shaped anthropology as a discipline. Students read classic and contemporary theory alongside ethnographic cases, learning how concepts such as culture, structure, function, symbol, practice, habitus, discourse, materiality, ontology, race, gender, coloniality, and more-than-human relations become tools for explanation. The course sequence expands into a granular, research-ready syllabus that emphasizes critique, application, and theory-building.');

